  "text": {
    "work": "work",
    "card": "Practice a three-strand braid, crossing and undoing one step.",
    "braid": "braid practice",
    "cord": "three colored strands",
    "wrong_stage": "Use the crossing or undo offer for the current braid stage.",
    "free_hand": "Put down an object so a hand is free for the practice control.",
    "howto_braid": "Use the fixed practice control to advance the attached indexed depiction one whole crossing, or undo only its last crossing. Fixed L C R letters name left, center and right. Fixed colored A B C references name the original red, blue and gold strands. Starting order ABC changes through BAC, BCA, CBA, CAB, ACB and ABC. At even stages0,2,4 choose left-over-center; at1,3,5 choose right-over-center. The front strand goes over with a nonzero depth gap. Each stage retains all previous crossing rows and moves the remaining loose ends; stage6 keeps six crossings although its order matches stage0. Undo removes just the lowest crossing. This attached instructional model uses connected segmented capsules and approximate indexed poses; it does not conserve quantitative rope length, simulate continuous rope motion or tension, secure knots, consume stock, detach an output or create anything to pick up or carry. The hand touches a practice control, without an anatomical braid-working/contact guarantee.",
    "fully_braided": "The six crossings are complete; undo a crossing first.",
    "fully_unbraided": "The strands are already uncrossed; braid a crossing first."
  },
